    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Apply or disable video stabilization.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target segment id\r\n          --level TEXT        Stabilization level: recommended (balanced stability/crop,\r\n                              default), minimum-crop (least crop), or most-stable (strongest\r\n                              stabilization)\r\n          --disable           Disable video stabilization on the segment\r\n          --timeout <duration> \r\n                              Algorithm wait timeout; explicit unit required (us, ms, s, min).\r\n                              Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min; bare numbers and m are\r\n                              invalid.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Apply the default recommended level (balanced stability and crop)\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video stabilize --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Use the minimum-crop level: less crop, weaker stabilization\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video stabilize --seg-id <UUID> --level minimum-crop\r\n  # Use the most-stable level: strongest stabilization, may crop more\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video stabilize --seg-id <UUID> --level most-stable\r\n  # Turn video stabilization off\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video stabilize --seg-id <UUID> --disable\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Apply or disable video stabilization.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target segment id\r\n          --level TEXT        Stabilization level: recommended (balanced stability/crop,\r\n                              default), minimum-crop (least crop), or most-stable (strongest\r\n                              stabilization)\r\n          --disable           Disable video stabilization on the segment\r\n          --timeout <duration> \r\n                              Algorithm wait timeout; explicit unit required (us, ms, s, min).\r\n                              Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min; bare numbers and m are\r\n                              invalid.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Apply the default recommended level (balanced stability and crop)\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video stabilize --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Use the minimum-crop level: less crop, weaker stabilization\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video stabilize --seg-id <UUID> --level minimum-crop\r\n  # Use the most-stable level: strongest stabilization, may crop more\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video stabilize --seg-id <UUID> --level most-stable\r\n  # Turn video stabilization off\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video stabilize --seg-id <UUID> --disable\r\n",
